  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving water availability and safety through optimised irrigation and fertiliser application by hydroponic growers in Vietnam</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In this pilot project, a solution is provided for the problems of low water availability and groundwater polution in the greenhouse sector in Vietnam. By re-using drain water, 10 to 35% water and up to 50% fertilisers can be saved. To ensure diseases don&#x2019;t spread through the production area, the drain water needs to be disinfected. To ensure plants receive the right amount of nutrients a fertiliser mixer is required. This can be achieved using the VitaLite and FertiMix technologies. The pilot project will demonstrate this on two farms in Lam Dong province, Vietnam. Eliminating drain water leaching into the environment will have a positive effect on the water quality of groundwater in in Lam Dong province and fresh water further downstream the Dong Nai River basin by elimination contamination of these water systems by excess fertilisers. The project is executed by a consortium led by Fresh Studions, including HollandDoor, Ridder Group and Royal Brinkman.</narrative>
  </description>
